# Documentation Maintenance

Three markdown docs live at the project root. Keep them current as you work.

## Files

- `PRD.md` — Product requirements, features, milestones
- `BUG_SQUASH.md` — Every bug found/fixed gets an entry
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` — Directory map, key decisions, module summaries, conventions

## When to Update

| Trigger | Action |
|---------|--------|
| New feature started | Add feature row to PRD §3.1, update ARCHITECTURE module table |
| Bug found | Add entry under "Active Bugs" in BUG_SQUASH |
| Bug fixed | Move entry to "Resolved", update stats row |
| New file/folder created | Update ARCHITECTURE directory tree |
| Tech decision made | Add row to ARCHITECTURE "Key Decisions" |
| Milestone reached | Update PRD §6 milestone status |
| Stack chosen or changed | Update PRD §5 and ARCHITECTURE conventions |

## Rules

1. Update the `Last updated` date in each file you touch.
2. Use the existing templates — don't restructure the docs.
3. Increment BUG IDs sequentially (BUG-001, BUG-002, …).
4. Feature IDs follow F-XXX format.
5. Keep ARCHITECTURE directory tree accurate after any file/folder change.
